 janky CGI  was always a big and consistent  complaint about the film and it's not  unfounded either especially during the  final fight between t'challa and Michael  B Jordan's killmonger underneath wakanda  to be fair this issue isn't a problem  with black panther or wakanda forever  specifically as a lot of recent  Blockbusters have been burdened with an  overabundance of shoddy VFX work  nonetheless a lot of the CGI and black  panther wakanda forever feels  undercooked with fans on Tick Tock  comparing Riri Williams overly shiny  Iron Heart armor to a Power Rangers  costume honestly it's a point that's  hard to argue with despite ironheart's  otherwise welcome addition to the cast  one of the chief complaints lobbed at  the Marvel Cinematic Universe especially  since 2012's Avengers is the overly  quippy and self-referential Whedon speak  Batman is playing Galaga  thought we wouldn't notice  but we did worse that kind of patented  overly snarky and irreverent dialogue  that the MCU has traded in for over a  decade has been seeping into other  movies as well becoming the de facto  mode of conversation for way too many  Blockbusters this has led to an  inevitable backlash towards the MCU by  critics and fans alike especially  considering its ubiquity across the  entire entertainment industry fans  eventually started complaining about how  the MCU now had far too many jokes the  stakes started to feel non-existent and  every character had the same quippy  attitude despite their disparate  backgrounds and Origins luckily many  fans were happy to discover that black  panther wakanda forever had a much more  serious tone it makes sense considering  the entire film is grappling with heavy  topics like grief the devastating  effects of imperialism and the death of  its previous star hanging over it  unfortunately some fans didn't  appreciate the change in tone or at the  very least didn't appreciate just how  dark and depressive it got one Twitter  user wrote that the mood was too serious  another Twitter user comedically  showcased the change in tone and  perspective between the two black  panther films by showing two very  different moments in the same James  Corden skit there was probably no way  given the unfortunate behind the scenes  circumstances of the film that wakanda  forever would be as fun as the first  black panther however it also makes  sense that many fans would rather have  come to watch an Escapist fantasy rather  than a sobering meditation on Grief and  loss  another of the small handful of  criticisms faced by the first black  panther film was about the inclusion of  a good guy CIA agent Everett Ross the  concept feels disingenuous as in the  real world the CIA has been at the  Forefront of toppling many  democratically elected governments  around the world this has particularly  affected nations in Africa and Central  and South America cultures that inspired  wakanda and talocon the U.S has played a  part in stripping those nations of their  natural resources which is not too  dissimilar to Western Nations desire to  obtain vibranium in the films even the  Black Panther films in the MCU don't shy  away from the agency's terrible and  imperialist atrocities it's a major plot  point in Black Panther wakanda forever  that the US government operating via  agent Ross's ex-wife CIA director  Valentina Allegra de Fontaine is behind  a plan to steal both wakanda and  talocon's vibranium by any means  necessary a Twitter user stated the  issues with the film's political framing  pretty plainly in an insightful tweet  absolutely hilarious how wakanda forever  seamlessly goes from this dangerous  indigenous extremist wants his land back  that's messed up to anyway let's check  in with our lovable CIA scam this is not  to say that there isn't any Nuance in  coogler and the mcu's depiction of the  CIA but it could still do better in  grappling with the issue  the cast member who stands out most of  all in the Black Panther films is Angela  Bassett who plays t'challa and shuri's  mother the wise and Regal Queen ramonda  in Black Panther wakanda forever  bassett's Queen ramonda has taken over  diplomatic Affairs for wakanda after  t'challa's untimely death she does this  as powerful Western Nations like France  and the United States attempt to  undermine wakanda's sovereignty and gain  access to their vibranium these attempts  lead those governments to the ocean  where they find Neymar's Kingdom of  talocon unbeknownst to the rest of the  world namor's people have their own  reserve of vibranium as well because of  this Neymar attempts to broker a truce  with wakanda which doesn't go well and  eventually Neymar attacks wakanda and  drowns Queen raimonda I need to know  this one was an intentional move by the  filmmakers to make viewers upset the  sadness and Melancholy were the desired  effect Ryan coogler wanted and he  certainly did succeed if social media is  anything to go by just see the reaction  from Twitter users reacting with  statements like Queen Mother get up to  get this out of the way up front when it  comes to portraying shuri's Journey from  grief to her acceptance of the mantle of  black panther Leticia Wright absolutely  kills it in wakanda Forever she more  than steps into the vibranium shoes left  by Chadwick Boseman as she showcases a  wide range of emotions while handling  the action scenes with immense skill not  only is she asked to do more in the  sequel but she Nails every aspect of her  performance outside the movie though  it's been disheartening for many fans to  find out that between Black Panther and  wakanda forever Wright took to spreading  anti-vaxx and bigoted anti-trans  conspiracy theories upon facing backlash  for her comments she only doubled down  rather than apologizing or retracting  them there have also been reports  alleging that she was responsible for a  coveted scare on the wakanda forever set  because of all this some fans  understandably